But being stressed out is usually something you feel when you have too much stuff to do.

101
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:41,900
So maybe you can be stressed out because of school, like in your case, or maybe at work you have a lot of things to do or a project to finish, right?

102
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:54,600
Exactly and I just want to point out here that you can say I'm stressed or I'm feeling stressed but commonly in spoken English, so when you're talking to your friends, you hear this much more often, stressed out.

103
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:56,700
Stressed out, he's really stressed out lately.

104
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:04,640
So we're stressed out or another word that kind of means the same is this is nerve-wracking.

105
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:09,700
Nerve-wracking, so nerves are those things in our body that help us feel things, right?

106
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:15,560
And so something that racks our nerves makes us very, very tense, very anxious, very uncomfortable.

107
00:05:15,710 --> 00:05:17,490
