Exactly.

251
00:11:56,080 --> 00:12:00,920
So you want to cheer up your friends or maybe if you're feeling a bit down, a family member will try and cheer you up.

252
00:12:01,150 --> 00:12:02,710
Do you need someone to cheer you up, Marco?

253
00:12:03,590 --> 00:12:03,920
Yes, I do.

254
00:12:05,570 --> 00:12:08,480
Let's go have a drink and eat some popcorn and be cheered up.

255
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:11,010
That's what cheers me up or chocolate always cheers me up.

256
00:12:11,050 --> 00:12:12,190
Oh, I know there's some of that.

257
00:12:12,750 --> 00:12:13,150
All right.

258
00:12:13,370 --> 00:12:20,670
So we've taken a look at a lot of great phrases, but the last sentence of the dialogue is maybe a little bit strange, right?

259
00:12:20,790 --> 00:12:23,310
When she says, you are something else.

260
00:12:23,470 --> 00:12:23,890
You know that?

261
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:26,360
Something what?

262
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:26,880
Is she an alien?

263
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:28,360
Is she a monkey?

264
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:30,220
What does she mean when she says you are something else?

265
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:31,100
That's a great question.

266
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:37,640
Well, this might be a little bit hard to understand at first, but she's saying, I can't believe you.

267
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:38,680
She's like, there's no one like you.

268
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:39,740
You're really something else.

269
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:40,340
You know that?

270
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:45,090
It's kind of like a joke, but what she's saying is, I can't believe you.

271
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:48,250
You just want to go on and encourage me to find another boy.

272
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:49,750
You're unbelievable.

273
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:54,630
So it could be, is it on a positive note or can it be both positive and negative?

274
00:12:54,970 --> 00:13:00,870
Well, here we've got two friends who are using it, so it's a positive note, but she's kind of making fun of her saying, I can't believe you.

275
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:02,680
But it can be negative.

276
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:03,680
It can be more negative.

277
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:09,800
Like if you're fighting with her boyfriend and her boyfriend cheats on her and she's like, you're really something else.

278
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:10,800
You know that?

279
00:13:11,930 --> 00:13:12,800
It's like, there's no comparison.

280
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:13,800
You're the worst.

281
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:14,800
Yeah, exactly.

282
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:20,840
So yeah, it really depends on how this is used and what the tone of voice is, so how someone says it.

283
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:25,800
But in this case, I think it's kind of a joke, but it's the positive.

284
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:26,800
Right.

285
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:27,800
Very interesting.

286
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:36,880
It's very spoken English, as you say, because all the words that we see there, they're pretty simple, but the context or the connotation, the meaning is very, very different from the actual words.

287
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:37,880
Exactly.

288
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:38,880
All right.

289
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:43,780
So let's listen to this dialogue for the last time and then we'll come back and talk a little bit more.

290
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:51,200
Okay.

291
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:52,420
I'll talk to you later.

292
00:13:52,860 --> 00:13:53,240
Bye.

293
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:55,960
Carrie, are you okay?

294
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:57,240
You seem a bit down.

295
00:13:57,800 --> 00:13:59,360
I just got off the phone with my boyfriend.

296
00:14:00,430 --> 00:14:03,070
He's always getting upset and losing his temper over nothing.

297
00:14:03,730 --> 00:14:05,290
It's so hard to talk to him at times.

298
00:14:06,870 --> 00:14:09,810
Maybe it's just that he's stressed out from working or something.

299
00:14:10,450 --> 00:14:12,590
He does have a pretty nerve-wracking job, you know?

300
00:14:12,990 --> 00:14:15,930
Yeah, but he's always in a really foul mood.

301
00:14:16,590 --> 00:14:23,210
I try to find out what's bothering him or get him to talk about his day, but he always shuts down and brushes me off.

302
00:14:23,810 --> 00:14:25,090
Men are like that, you know.

303
00:14:25,470 --> 00:14:32,070
They can feel nervous, anxious, or on edge, and the only way they can express it is by trying to hide it through aggressiveness.

304
00:14:32,790 --> 00:14:33,470
I guess you're right.

305
00:14:34,260 --> 00:14:35,460
What do you think I should do?

306
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,520
He wasn't always this grouchy, you know.

307
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:38,720
Talk to him.

308
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:40,240
Try to cheer him up when he's down.

309
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:43,740
And if that doesn't work, I say get rid of him and get a new one.

310
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:45,660
You are something else, you know that?

311
00:14:52,390 --> 00:14:55,510
So, Catherine, are you a grouchy person? Are you happy?

312
00:14:55,870 --> 00:14:56,220
Do you have a bad temper?

313
00:14:56,220 --> 00:14:59,970
Oh, these are, well, very interesting questions, Marco.

314
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:02,690
Thank you for asking. No, the first time, am I grouchy?

315
00:15:02,850 --> 00:15:03,250
No, not very.

316
00:15:03,510 --> 00:15:04,220
Only before 9am.

317
00:15:05,290 --> 00:15:05,990
You're not a morning person.

318
00:15:06,170 --> 00:15:08,650
Not a morning person, so I'm very grouchy in the morning.

319
00:15:08,970 --> 00:15:11,770
But I'm generally pretty good about losing my temper.

320
00:15:11,930 --> 00:15:13,010
It doesn't happen very often.

321
00:15:13,220 --> 00:15:14,220
Oh, really?

322
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:18,150
But I do get frustrated with things like tapping or when people eat with their mouth open.

323
00:15:18,450 --> 00:15:19,750
Oh, yeah, that's terrible.

324
00:15:20,350 --> 00:15:21,210
I hate that as well.

325
00:15:21,590 --> 00:15:22,220
Yeah, I can't stand it.

326
00:15:22,330 --> 00:15:24,630
Or I really don't like when people bite their nails.

327
00:15:26,290 --> 00:15:28,170
It also makes me lose my temper.

328
00:15:28,550 --> 00:15:28,770
I don't know.

329
00:15:28,870 --> 00:15:31,430
It more than makes me lose my temper, it's kind of annoying, right?

330
00:15:31,570 --> 00:15:31,950
It is annoying.

331
00:15:32,230 --> 00:15:33,670
So what makes you really lose your temper?

332
00:15:33,890 --> 00:15:35,670
We say, what makes you blow your top?

333
00:15:36,330 --> 00:15:37,030
Think about a volcano.

334
00:15:37,390 --> 00:15:38,630
Really grinds my gears.

335
00:15:40,610 --> 00:15:46,070
I would say the worst is when somebody lies to me, like straight in my face.

336
00:15:46,250 --> 00:15:47,270
Like I know they're lying.

337
00:15:47,430 --> 00:15:50,220
I know you're lying and you still just lie straight at me.

338
00:15:50,620 --> 00:15:51,060
I agree.

339
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:56,220
So what's something that really cheers you up? Because we talked about like going out with a friend maybe helps you cheer up.

340
00:15:56,220 --> 00:16:00,220
But is there one thing, some kind of remedy?

341
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:04,220
I actually like to go shopping when I'm feeling a bit sad.

342
00:16:04,220 --> 00:16:05,220
Really?

343
00:16:05,220 --> 00:16:08,260
Yeah. I mean, I won't buy anything like clothes or anything like that.

344
00:16:08,460 --> 00:16:11,720
Usually I'll get maybe something for somebody else or for the house or something.

345
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:12,220
It's very strange.

346
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:13,220
Helps you like clear your mind.

347
00:16:13,220 --> 00:16:17,200
Yeah, it's just like walking around and spending a little bit of money.

348
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:17,580
I don't know.

349
00:16:17,700 --> 00:16:18,220
It's kind of a good remedy.

350
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:19,660
Yeah, I think so.

351
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:20,240
What about you?

352
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:21,140
What cheers you up?

353
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:23,220
I kind of like to organize things.

354
00:16:23,220 --> 00:16:24,220
Really?

355
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:29,170
Yeah. So if I'm really angry or really upset about something, I'll alphabetize all of my books.

356
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:30,220
Oh, wow.

357
00:16:30,450 --> 00:16:31,510
Yeah. So A to Z.

358
00:16:32,770 --> 00:16:32,950
Wow.

359
00:16:33,130 --> 00:16:42,220
See, everyone has different remedies. So come to our website, englishpod.com. Tell us what makes you angry, what makes you lose your temper or what really cheers you up, what makes you happy.

360
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:43,890
Or who cheers you up.

361
00:16:43,990 --> 00:16:48,070
So tell us who is someone you like to talk to when you're upset and how do they cheer you up?

362
00:16:48,230 --> 00:16:48,590
All right.

363
00:16:48,730 --> 00:16:53,930
We'll see you guys there. And also if you have questions, comments, suggestions, you can also leave them there in our comment section.

364
00:16:54,250 --> 00:16:54,910
Please do that.

365
00:16:55,110 --> 00:16:56,370
So that's all for today.

366
00:16:56,630 --> 00:16:57,110
Goodbye, everyone.

367
00:16:57,220 --> 00:17:06,064
Bye.
